    "guidance": "Preferred default among these policies when phase confidence is low and the state matches the demonstrated segment entry. It passed 10/12 in-distribution runs, with zero reported unconverged IK steps in all 12. Use with drawer_position >0.26 m, red visible and preferably acquired or in a demonstrated-style approach, and a current reachable red_goal. The destination-centered representation is intended for pad-relative placement; relocated-pad benefit is not validated. Avoid using it as the assumed solution to a far-displaced red pickup, blue displacement, obstruction, or unreachable goal. The two validation failures kept the drawer open (final 0.2935 and 0.2943 m) but left red off-pad, so an open drawer and clean IK are insufficient: monitor red support/containment, opening before support, red following retreat, and stale blue targeting. Handoff: confirm red is on the pad, no longer follows TCP, and drawer_position is still >0.26. Its supervised overlap can be handed to blue_insert while red is still held/touching because release context is included; established blue/TCP co-motion during initial lift is the least ambiguous nominal switch cue."
